Z||000000||count_iblis||01-05-2001||06:26 PM||||Ok a friend of mine just bought a 85 gt.  The guy that bought it says that it is an 85 1/2 model.  Now I know and you know that the 85 gt was the only Gt coupe, but this one strikes me as weird.  The car is a 5 speed.  Now the car has always been one owner from what he says.  I was like ok but did you change out the transmission?  He said no and I almost got into an arguing match with the guy.  So I get into the car and look at the plate that has the shift pattern on it.  THe pattern is for a 4 speed.  I mean the transmission was replace right, and there wasnt a 85 gt 5 speed right?  Just wanna make sure.  The car is cool though overall.  The best feature I like about it is that its push button!  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-05-2001||07:08 PM||||Check the VIN to be sure of model year. I bet the tranny isn't original. No 5 speed v-6 in '85.||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||01-05-2001||07:18 PM||||We just did that, and the vin says it is an 85 gt.  So it had to be changed out.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||01-05-2001||07:18 PM||||Take a look and see if it's an Isuzu or a Getrag. If it's an Isuzu, there's no way GM put it in there. Well, Actually I guess anything is possible.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
